  "definitions": {
    "d1": "100*|neff_fdfd-neff_exact|/|neff_exact|; one maximum gate per geometry, not per reported eigenvalue. Theory supplies the eigensolver shift guess, so this checks a theory-assisted branch, not blind mode identification.",
    "d2": "Reflection: RMSE of |Gamma|, norm(Gamma_fdtd-Gamma_exact)/norm(Gamma_exact), wrapped phase RMSE in degrees; separate incident calibration, predefined interface and axial Yee de-embedding, retained frequency/signal mask.",
    "d3": "Five exact TEM sheet impedances; reflection magnitude/phase RMSE after separate Tukey incident/reflected time gates and axial Yee de-embedding. Long lossless-inductor check is stability, not a separate reflection-accuracy reference.",
    "d4": "Two maximum relative-error identities for 4 W / 1 W scaling and accepted-versus-incident normalization, each <=5e-12. These are implementation consistency, not an independent electromagnetic reference. Raw powers are reported in W.",
    "d5": "Primary gated SAR reference is the continuous halfspace cell-average. Two gates on worst errors across 14 frequencies and 16 points/frequency; Yee-collocated and continuous-centre references are report-only.",
    "d6": "Short-circuited slab impedance reflection; independent incident run and predefined-front-face axial Yee de-embedding; magnitude max error, phase max degrees, complex relative L2.",
    "d7": "Five independent continuous-medium recursive Fresnel stacks, same requested first interface, averaged/staircased. 150 FDTD frequencies/mode; 2001 dense analytical plot points are not additional simulations. Phase retains |Gamma_exact|>=0.02. No numerical acceptance gate.",
    "d8": "Far-field directivity RMS and peak-directivity absolute error; near-field L2 only where analytical |Ez| is at least 1% of peak. Prescribed excitation is shared with the independent electromagnetic reference; no fitted trace shift/scale.",
    "d9": "10*log10(FDTD RCS / independent Mie RCS), 34 sampled frequencies, incident-plane-wave normalization; includes voxelization and NTFF error.",
    "d10": "Independent Mie absorption cross-section and absorbed power, both relative errors <=8%. 1g/10g mass-averaged SAR peaks in W/kg are report-only; no mass-average analytical gate or fresh 0.5-mm refinement is present.",
    "d11": "Independent exact cylindrical series, two polarizations; interior local SAR excludes the two-cell interface band and retains analytical SAR >=5% peak. Local L2 and maximum pointwise relative error; power W/m and cross-section m are gated as relative errors. All-cell metrics are report-only. TE and fat/skin extend rather than reproduce the literature muscle TM case.",
    "d12": "Independent Capoglu echo propagation driven by saved sampled source differentiated by finite differences; fixed common predelay and source-edge location. Max/RMS of waveform difference divided by analytical peak over reduced time 0–100 ps.",
    "d13": "Bare PEC image theory / independently coded coated-slab impedance. One complex least-squares scale per source/frequency across both cuts removes common amplitude/phase; field/power peak-normalized errors and directivity remain gated, absolute source calibration does not.",
    "d14": "Independent Aden–Kerker Debye-core/Lorentz-shell Mie RCS; norm(RCS_fdtd-RCS_exact)/norm(RCS_exact)*100 and 10*log10 RCS ratio. Coarse 4-mm/160^3 baseline, 87 sampled frequencies; dense analytical curve is plot-only. No numerical acceptance gate."
  },
